ade, in largely the same way: pashm combed by hand on the Changthang plateau, spun on a charkha, woven on wood, finished by people whose parents did the same work."}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 text-[0.9375rem] leading-relaxed text-mocha","children":"What has changed is who we sell to. For most of our history the shawls left the valley through intermediaries who neither knew nor cared who had woven them. Now they go directly, with a certificate carrying the weaver’s name — which is the part of this business we are most pleased about."}]]}]]}]}],"$L8","$L9"],null,"$La"]}],{},null,false]},null,false]},null,false],"$Lb",false]],"m":"$undefined","G":["$c",[]],"s":false,"S":true}
